U; curve b: 8.72 U; curve c: 12.76 U) and reaction time on yield of nicotinamide. (c) Reusability of NHase@Co-Cys on nicotinamide production.
The reusability of immobilized enzyme was a major advantage compared with the free form, which realized the recycling and reduced the cost. Thanks to the improvement of microenvironment after immobilization, and the interaction between cobalt-type enzyme and cobalt ions, NHase $@$ Co-Cys remained $83.85\%$ of the original enzyme activity after reusing for 10 times (Fig. 9c) [61, 72]. The activity decrease of NHase $@$ Co-Cys might be due to the diffusional limitations of both reactants and products which imposed by the deposits of reaction product accumulated on the matrix surface. These reasons caused mass transfer restrictions to the protein molecules [73, 74]. Meanwhile, the shaking conditions could also affect the conformation of the molecule and lead the inactivation of NHase $@$ Co-Cys during the long reaction term [34, 75, 76]. The favorable reusability of immobilized NHase might provide a cost-effective alternative for industrial production of nicotinamide.
## 3.8. Determination of kinetic parameters of NHase
On the basis of Michaelis-Menten equation and Lineweaver-Burk plot, the kinetic parameters of free NHase and NHase@Co-Cys were determined. The Km value of free NHase and NHase $@$ Co-Cys was $10.23~\mathrm{mM}$ and $18.67~\mathrm{mM}$ respectively. The results indicated that the affinity between the substrate and enzyme molecule have a certain decrease after immobilization. On the other hand, the Vmax value of NHase@Co-Cys (1.35 mmol/min)was larger than that of free NHase (0.63 mmol/min). The kinetic parameters of NHase@Co-Cys were improved compared with other immobilized NHase [66], which might be attributed to the local enrichment of substrates in porous structures of NHase@Co-Cys.
## 4. Conclusions
In this work, Co-Cys BioMOFs materials were successfully synthesized and employed to immobilize NHase via a simple in-situ encapsulation method. The obtained NHase@Co-Cys exhibited excellent encapsulation yield and specific activity. Benefit from the special structural features of BioMOFs materials and the effect of cobalt ion on the activity of NHase, NHase $@$ Co-Cys exhibited improvement in enzyme properties and stabilities when compared with the free enzyme. In addition, when NHase $@$ Co-Cys was used in the preparation of nicotinamide, the reusability was enhanced. Thus, NHase@Co-Cys is an effective approach for enzyme immobilization and the enhancement of properties and stabilities provided an opportunity to broaden its application in industrial field.
